          "description": "Unshaded first-quadrant graph with positive arrowheads, monetary vertical axis, x horizontal axis, three labelled ticks on each axis, pale grid lines, and two coloured straight lines with matching legend strokes. Neither the origin nor the intersection has a point label or marker.",
          "mathematics": "Revenue is reconstructed as R(x)=25x and cost as C(x)=1000+5x, both drawn for 0≤x≤70. Major grid steps are 20 books horizontally and 500 dollars vertically. Revenue passes through the labelled grid intersections (20,500), (40,1000) and (60,1500). The cost intercept is 1000. Its intended gradient 5 is corroborated by teacher answer 42(a); the source does not supply a second explicitly labelled cost coordinate.",
